1
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:12,650
[Last Episode] Oh, man! This is hilarious!

2
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:18,770
Oh, my stomach hurts.
I laughed so hard my stomach hurts.

3
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:33,670
I shouldn't have come back.

4
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:42,530
I laughed so much that I'm thirsty. I need some water.

5
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:01,530
Choi Yun announced his plans to get married.

6
00:01:01,530 --> 00:01:03,200
What a selfish guy.

7
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,360
If things don't work out with him,
she's going to be a widow.

8
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:09,610
Why doesn't he put himself in her shoes for once?

9
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:11,640
Mother and son are so much alike
in their selfish ways.

10
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:14,770
Looks like it runs in the family.

11
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,860
I signed the publishing agreement.

12
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:22,020
The book will go on sale in a few days.

13
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:25,780
It'll turn the world upside-down.
Just wait a couple of days.

14
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:27,530
I'll treat you to a meal then.

15
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:41,520
Just like someone thrown away like garbage ought to,

16
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:45,160
I should have lived like garbage,

17
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:49,740
then disappear quietly, like garbage.

18
00:02:08,350 --> 00:02:09,860
Excuse me.

19
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:13,240
Excuse me. But would you happen to know
where building 16-1 is?

20
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:18,220
Is this it?

21
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:32,500
Excuse me. Anyone home?

22
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:35,990
Muhyeok!

23
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:39,970
Muhyeok!

24
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:46,790
It's me. It's me, Jiyeong.

25
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,700
Don't you recognize me?

26
00:02:57,530 --> 00:02:58,900
Muhyeok!

27
00:03:19,010 --> 00:03:20,350
Muhyeok!

28
00:03:22,210 --> 00:03:28,380
I worried every day that you might have already died.

29
00:03:41,110 --> 00:03:44,840
I broke up with Jason.

30
00:03:45,946 --> 00:03:50,995
I told Jason that I could never trade stuff with money,

31
00:03:50,995 --> 00:03:58,150
even though it's as much as Australia.
I made a mistake.

32
00:03:58,150 --> 00:03:59,730
Let's go, Muhyeok.

33
00:03:59,730 --> 00:04:01,890
I've been asking around.

34
00:04:01,890 --> 00:04:05,560
There's a famous doctor in Germany who Jason knows.

35
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:08,790
I told him about your condition,

36
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:11,700
and it's advised that you give surgery a go.

37
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:15,150
He said he'd find a way to keep you alive.

38
00:04:15,150 --> 00:04:16,980
Let's give it a try.

39
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:24,750
Let's do all we can. Let's try everything, Muhyeok.

40
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:37,560
[Cha Muhyeok]

41
00:04:54,290 --> 00:04:57,120
The only ones available are in the afternoon?

42
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:59,680
Fine, we'll take that flight.

43
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:04,810
Mine and Cha Muhyeok. Danny Anderson.

44
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,470
Who's she?

45
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:25,030
Someone you know?

46
00:05:30,710 --> 00:05:32,690
When did you get here?

47
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:37,300
Go home. It's cold.

48
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:41,550
Go.

49
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,250
Hey, Yun.

50
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:34,800
Where are you?

51
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:37,930
Outside Muhyeok's house.

52
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:42,750
Why did you go there?

53
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:45,870
I had something to say to him.

54
00:06:45,870 --> 00:06:48,490
I had something to say to Muhyeok.

55
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:54,100
Did you get to see him?

56
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:58,660
Yes, I did.

57
00:07:01,050 --> 00:07:02,480
Eunchae.

58
00:07:06,330 --> 00:07:07,990
All right.

59
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:13,580
Say what you need to say to him,
and I'll see you later.

60
00:07:13,580 --> 00:07:14,900
Okay.

61
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:28,340
Send the reporters off.

62
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:29,560
Yes, ma'am.

63
00:07:40,010 --> 00:07:43,530
What on earth were you thinking?

64
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:48,920
Who on earth makes a wedding announcement like that?

65
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:53,430
How will I ever face Eunchae's family again?

66
00:07:53,430 --> 00:07:58,060
Don't you think you should've at least
given us a heads up?

67
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:00,800
Mom, you're the one who taught me this.

68
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:01,730
What?

69
00:08:01,730 --> 00:08:06,970
If anyone throws a punch,
to return the favor with twice the fury.

70
00:08:06,970 --> 00:08:11,300
That being weak isn't pitiful, it's bad.

71
00:08:12,110 --> 00:08:16,670
What? Why on earth would you bring that up now?

72
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,910
That jerk who made me this way...

73
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:25,140
I want to stab him in the chest.

74
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:28,740
You what? I didn't hear.
What did you just say?

75
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:31,240
I'm saying you taught me wrong.

76
00:08:33,830 --> 00:08:38,300
Yeah. That's not right.

77
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,790
That wasn't the right thing to do.

78
00:08:40,790 --> 00:08:44,060
I should've just suffered alone.

79
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:48,720
It's all your fault, Mom. You didn't raise me right.

80
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:51,980
Yun, how can you say that to your mom?

81
00:08:55,850 --> 00:08:57,950
You taught me the wrong life lessons.

82
00:08:57,950 --> 00:08:59,010
Yun!

83
00:08:59,010 --> 00:09:02,130
You said I should never let what I hold dear be taken.

84
00:09:02,130 --> 00:09:04,160
To never give in to anyone.

85
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:06,210
Why did you teach me that?

86
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:08,160
Yun!

87
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:11,120
To avoid losing you...

88
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:14,010
To avoid losing Eunchae...

89
00:09:17,890 --> 00:09:20,430
Do you know what I'm doing?

90
00:09:20,950 --> 00:09:22,340
Son!

91
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:30,260
Sorry.

92
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:33,430
I'm sorry, Muhyeok.

93
00:09:34,990 --> 00:09:38,000
I was wrong.

94
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,620
I should be punished.

95
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:43,140
Forgive me.

96
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:51,640
I'll never leave you ever again.

97
00:09:52,650 --> 00:09:55,930
No matter what happens, let's never part, Muhyeok.

98
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:06,120
From now on, we'll be together till death do us part.

99
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:09,100
Let's never part again, okay?

100
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,250
Muhyeok!

101
00:14:00,470 --> 00:14:01,970
Yes, Yun.

102
00:14:01,970 --> 00:14:03,500
Where are you?

103
00:14:04,310 --> 00:14:07,000
I'm at Muhyeok's house.

104
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,320
You're still not done talking?

105
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:13,960
No, we haven't finished talking.

106
00:14:16,870 --> 00:14:21,590
I have something to say and he has something to say.

107
00:14:23,190 --> 00:14:26,220
No. We're not done yet.

108
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:28,000
All right.

109
00:15:11,090 --> 00:15:14,880
Are you still at Muhyeok's place?

110
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:16,530
Yeah.

111
00:15:16,530 --> 00:15:18,240
Okay, I got it.

112
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:41,720
I'm coming back tomorrow.

113
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:46,446
And the day after that, and the day after that,

114
00:16:46,446 --> 00:16:49,380
and all the days after...

115
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:53,820
I'll look at you till I get sick of you.

116
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:58,700
Until I stop wanting to see you,
until I get sick of you,

117
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:00,930
I will continue coming.

118
00:17:00,930 --> 00:17:04,385
I won't let you order me around,

119
00:17:04,385 --> 00:17:07,840
asking me to come or go as your heart desires.

120
00:17:10,130 --> 00:17:13,690
To come and go as Yun asks.

121
00:17:13,690 --> 00:17:16,520
To come and go as you ask.

122
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:20,420
I'm not a leaf to be blown to and fro

123
00:17:20,420 --> 00:17:23,630
based on your desires.

124
00:17:24,810 --> 00:17:31,230
I, too, have my own desires,

125
00:17:31,230 --> 00:17:34,860
things I wish to possess,

126
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:37,420
and things I want to accomplish.

127
00:17:38,990 --> 00:17:41,490
I even have things I try so hard to hold back

128
00:17:41,490 --> 00:17:44,440
but end up unable to.

129
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,350
Do you know that?

130
00:17:46,350 --> 00:17:50,220
I too am a human being who has feelings like you two!

131
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:53,210
You didn't know that, did you?

132
00:17:53,210 --> 00:17:57,140
I, too, am human like the two of you!

133
00:18:03,870 --> 00:18:05,400
I love you.

134
00:18:10,490 --> 00:18:12,250
I love you.

135
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:15,830
I love you.

136
00:18:19,150 --> 00:18:21,000
I love you.

137
00:18:22,870 --> 00:18:24,980
I love you, Mister.

138
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:30,750
I love you. I love you.

139
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:35,050
I love you. I love you!

140
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:43,120
I love you! I love you!

141
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:48,930
I love you.

142
00:18:49,930 --> 00:18:55,000
I love you. I love you, Mister.

143
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,200
I love you.

144
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:03,100
I love you, Mister.

145
00:19:17,290 --> 00:19:18,780
I love you.

146
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,460
I love you.

147
00:19:27,350 --> 00:19:28,930
I love you.

148
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:44,540
I shouldn't have come back.

149
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:53,540
Just like someone thrown away like garbage ought to,

150
00:19:53,540 --> 00:19:56,440
I should have lived like garbage,

151
00:19:56,440 --> 00:20:01,670
then disappear quietly, like garbage.

152
00:20:29,630 --> 00:20:33,730
I won't come back.

153
00:20:35,070 --> 00:20:37,270
Ever.

154
00:20:37,270 --> 00:20:42,430
I won't ever come back to Eunchae.

155
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:47,320
Please, take Eunchae.

156
00:21:38,150 --> 00:21:41,240
You have to forget about him. You silly girl.

157
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:45,320
You made a wedding announcement.

158
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,850
I know, right?

159
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:52,600
Oh, my. She feels like she's on fire.

160
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:58,960
Minchae, bring some fever medicine.

161
00:22:07,050 --> 00:22:08,300
Choi Yun.

162
00:22:12,510 --> 00:22:16,500
Eunchae left.

163
00:22:18,010 --> 00:22:19,700
She went home.

164
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:25,030
I didn't come for Eunchae. I came to see you.

165
00:22:25,030 --> 00:22:30,960
Come to think of it,
you and I never had a drink together.

166
00:23:19,070 --> 00:23:21,110
Since when were you such a caring guy?

167
00:23:22,860 --> 00:23:26,190
I've always been kind!

168
00:23:26,190 --> 00:23:31,250
If you hadn't provoked me, I'd have always been kind.

169
00:23:34,150 --> 00:23:38,100
If you hadn't provoked me,

170
00:23:38,100 --> 00:23:41,960
I'd have never known the love I had for Eunchae

171
00:23:41,960 --> 00:23:44,500
for my entire life.

172
00:23:46,490 --> 00:23:48,970
Eunchae and you.

173
00:23:48,970 --> 00:23:51,930
You and Eunchae.

174
00:23:51,930 --> 00:23:55,670
I would have never tried to break up you two,

175
00:23:55,670 --> 00:23:57,750
who love each other to death,

176
00:23:57,750 --> 00:24:00,760
and cause you all this pain.

177
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:05,350
You fell into your own trap.

178
00:24:05,350 --> 00:24:07,000
Did you know that?

179
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:09,790
I know.

180
00:24:11,690 --> 00:24:13,680
Pretend it's soju and drink it.

181
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:27,490
Shouldn't you be at the hospital?
What if something happens?

182
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:30,660
Pot calling the kettle black, huh?

183
00:24:35,380 --> 00:24:37,890
Don't you have something to say to me?

184
00:24:37,890 --> 00:24:43,520
After all, I took Eunchae and stabbed you in the back.

185
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:45,760
Don't want to say something to me?

186
00:24:47,580 --> 00:24:50,090
Nothing to say, really.

187
00:24:50,090 --> 00:24:53,840
I do have a few punches I wanted to dole out.

188
00:24:55,300 --> 00:24:56,870
Go ahead.

189
00:24:58,760 --> 00:25:02,130
If I hit you, you'd die.

190
00:25:03,060 --> 00:25:05,830
Well, didn't you always want to kill me anyway?

191
00:25:09,760 --> 00:25:15,190
Should we die together?

192
00:25:18,410 --> 00:25:20,750
Let's die together!

193
00:25:22,250 --> 00:25:27,480
We can die together and see what happens to Mom.

194
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:29,370
Let's die together.

195
00:25:30,100 --> 00:25:34,980
It'd be a lot better than the revenge you plotted.

196
00:25:39,750 --> 00:25:41,380
Mom.

197
00:25:42,660 --> 00:25:45,430
Me and Muhyeok are going to die.

198
00:25:47,200 --> 00:25:52,100
Your precious son, Yun.

199
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:56,120
And the son you tossed out like garbage,
Muhyeok, are dying together.

200
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:59,940
The Muhyeok that you abandoned
because you had no other choice...

201
00:26:02,220 --> 00:26:10,524
And the Yun who you adopted,
unable to fill that void Muhyeok left,

202
00:26:10,524 --> 00:26:13,000
are dying together.

203
00:26:17,240 --> 00:26:24,870
What did you just say?

204
00:26:26,870 --> 00:26:28,510
What did you just say?

205
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:33,750
My mom adopted me.

206
00:26:34,860 --> 00:26:37,200
I'm not her biological son.

207
00:26:39,490 --> 00:26:41,220
I was adopted.

208
00:26:42,320 --> 00:26:45,770
The only difference is that

209
00:26:45,770 --> 00:26:48,780
you were sent overseas,

210
00:26:48,780 --> 00:26:53,920
whereas I was fortunate enough to be adopted here.

211
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:56,330
There must have been a reason.

212
00:26:59,670 --> 00:27:05,130
After all, she's the kind of person
who'd give up her life for me,

213
00:27:05,130 --> 00:27:08,190
who isn't even really her own child.

214
00:27:09,690 --> 00:27:12,110
That's just the kind of person she is.

215
00:27:13,350 --> 00:27:16,340
There must have been a reason.

216
00:27:19,420 --> 00:27:28,080
For a person like my mom to abandon her own children...

217
00:27:31,340 --> 00:27:34,090
There must have been an unavoidable reason.

218
00:27:36,020 --> 00:27:39,850
I was so scared that I'd lose her to you,

219
00:27:39,850 --> 00:27:42,470
so I never told her you were back.

220
00:27:48,180 --> 00:27:51,080
I used to be a good guy.

221
00:27:55,100 --> 00:27:57,750
But you made me this way.

222
00:28:06,010 --> 00:28:09,300
I wanted to punish you.

223
00:28:14,700 --> 00:28:19,930
But because my heart was beating too fast, I didn't.

224
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:24,540
If I'd continued, I would have died earlier than you.

225
00:28:24,540 --> 00:28:26,620
So I couldn't do it.

226
00:28:29,500 --> 00:28:31,900
I'll go and tell her.

227
00:28:35,360 --> 00:28:38,370
No matter what,

228
00:28:41,090 --> 00:28:43,240
our mother

229
00:28:45,070 --> 00:28:47,190
will welcome you with open arms.

230
00:29:53,980 --> 00:29:56,760
Yun.

231
00:29:56,760 --> 00:30:00,780
Wake up! Yun!

232
00:30:11,248 --> 00:30:17,435
[Intensive Care Unit]

233
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:20,710
Yun... Yun...

234
00:30:25,610 --> 00:30:28,180
- You can't go in right now.
- What?

235
00:30:28,180 --> 00:30:30,060
Out of my way!

236
00:30:31,610 --> 00:30:33,380
I said you can't go in now.

237
00:30:33,380 --> 00:30:35,080
Who do you think you are?

238
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:38,090
I'm going to see my son! Move!

239
00:30:38,090 --> 00:30:42,070
Who do you think you are?
Get out of my way! Move!

240
00:30:42,070 --> 00:30:43,900
Why can't I go in?

241
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:48,400
Yun. Yun...

242
00:30:56,260 --> 00:30:59,740
After all, she's the kind of person
who'd give up her life for me,

243
00:30:59,740 --> 00:31:02,600
who isn't even really her own child.

244
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:06,230
That's just the kind of person she is.

245
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:10,810
Why did you abandon me?

246
00:31:12,620 --> 00:31:15,970
What were the unavoidable circumstances
that made you abandon me?

247
00:31:20,080 --> 00:31:26,130
You even raised a great son who wasn't your own.

248
00:31:27,570 --> 00:31:30,140
So why did you abandon your own kid?

249
00:31:34,370 --> 00:31:38,890
It wasn't just one. It was two.

250
00:31:40,750 --> 00:31:42,970
Why did you ditch me?

251
00:31:44,330 --> 00:31:49,690
What was it that made you abandon me? Why?

252
00:32:35,310 --> 00:32:41,860
Your dad was a married man with a family.

253
00:32:47,630 --> 00:32:49,480
It was me who threw you away.

254
00:32:53,500 --> 00:32:56,230
You and your sister.

255
00:32:56,230 --> 00:32:59,660
Babies who hadn't yet opened their eyes.

256
00:32:59,660 --> 00:33:01,840
It was I who threw you away.

257
00:33:03,710 --> 00:33:09,850
Compared to the suffering you'd have had to endure
as the children of a single mother

258
00:33:09,850 --> 00:33:12,530
and how you would ruin your mother's life...

259
00:33:12,530 --> 00:33:19,090
And compared to how unhappy you would have lived,

260
00:33:19,090 --> 00:33:30,610
I believed that was for the best for you two
and the best for your mother.

261
00:33:36,020 --> 00:33:39,030
She doesn't even know she had twins.

262
00:33:39,030 --> 00:33:42,450
She doesn't know anything.

263
00:33:42,450 --> 00:33:46,160
We told her that you died during childbirth.

264
00:33:46,160 --> 00:33:49,950
I told her that I personally spread
your ashes over a river.

265
00:33:49,950 --> 00:33:52,150
I told her that.

266
00:33:53,390 --> 00:33:59,320
I felt I should tell her the truth several times.

267
00:33:59,320 --> 00:34:02,460
But I didn't have the courage.

268
00:34:02,460 --> 00:34:09,110
I'd rather suffer alone than
to see Audrey suffer like that.

269
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:21,240
Say that again. What did you just say?

270
00:34:22,650 --> 00:34:31,130
She suffered so much because of your father.

271
00:34:31,130 --> 00:34:35,870
I couldn't see her go through anything like that again.

272
00:34:35,870 --> 00:34:43,000
I'd rather have died than
to watch her go through that again.

273
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:45,310
Then what about my life?

274
00:34:45,310 --> 00:34:50,290
Did you ever think of the lives of
me and my sister even once?

275
00:34:50,290 --> 00:34:55,120
Because of you, I hated my own mother!

276
00:34:55,120 --> 00:34:56,970
Despised my own mother!

277
00:34:56,970 --> 00:35:01,000
That's how I spent the last days of my life!

278
00:35:04,020 --> 00:35:05,600
I'm sorry.

279
00:35:13,600 --> 00:35:15,200
Sorry?

280
00:35:16,840 --> 00:35:18,960
Did you just say you were sorry?

281
00:35:24,200 --> 00:35:25,850
Sorry?

282
00:35:30,730 --> 00:35:36,270
For the rest of my life. I'll repent for my sins.

283
00:35:36,270 --> 00:35:41,830
I'll gladly accept any kind of punishment I receive.

284
00:35:43,850 --> 00:35:48,530
Yes, be punished.

285
00:35:50,540 --> 00:35:53,090
You must be punished.

286
00:36:57,250 --> 00:36:59,470
[Song Eunchae]

287
00:37:31,290 --> 00:37:33,430
[Text from Eunchae: "I love you. I love you."]

288
00:37:33,930 --> 00:37:39,590
I love you. I love you.

289
00:37:59,410 --> 00:38:01,040
Yun.

290
00:38:02,460 --> 00:38:05,960
Just this once...

291
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:13,130
Just this once, can't I be happily in love?

292
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:44,560
I'll do whatever it takes to save my Yun.

293
00:38:44,560 --> 00:38:49,500
I've lived long enough. It's fine.

294
00:38:49,500 --> 00:38:51,330
I'm fine with dying,

295
00:38:51,330 --> 00:38:53,750
but if my Yun were to die,
I won't be able to live, either.

296
00:38:53,750 --> 00:38:57,340
Doctor, if my Yun dies, I'll die, too.

297
00:38:59,060 --> 00:39:01,410
My mom adopted me.

298
00:39:01,410 --> 00:39:03,220
I was adopted.

299
00:39:04,470 --> 00:39:07,480
I was scared that you'd take my place.

300
00:39:09,010 --> 00:39:11,750
I used to be a good guy.

301
00:39:15,890 --> 00:39:18,080
But you made me this way.

302
00:39:22,740 --> 00:39:24,680
Open the door!

303
00:39:24,680 --> 00:39:26,290
Minju!

304
00:39:26,290 --> 00:39:28,740
Open the door! Please!

305
00:39:30,460 --> 00:39:32,050
Open the door!

306
00:39:50,710 --> 00:39:55,710
Let's meet in the next life.

307
00:39:55,710 --> 00:39:58,180
You and I

308
00:39:58,180 --> 00:40:02,050
weren't meant to be this time around.

309
00:40:21,540 --> 00:40:24,330
Mr. Cha. Will you take me home?

310
00:40:25,720 --> 00:40:32,400
I can't get ahold of Eunchae's dad
and I have to get Yun some things.

311
00:40:32,400 --> 00:40:34,490
Can you give me a ride?

312
00:41:03,500 --> 00:41:05,020
I...

313
00:41:06,990 --> 00:41:14,180
Mr. Cha, if I did anything wrong, please forgive me.

314
00:41:15,320 --> 00:41:19,510
Even if it was unforgivable.

315
00:41:20,750 --> 00:41:26,100
Take pity on an old woman like me and forgive me.

316
00:41:29,930 --> 00:41:32,670
I feel like I'm being punished.

317
00:41:33,520 --> 00:41:38,710
I committed the sins,
yet it's my children who are being punished.

318
00:41:38,710 --> 00:41:44,010
Just because they had a bad mom,
it feels like they're being punished.

319
00:41:49,070 --> 00:41:50,890
Will you give me something to eat?

320
00:41:51,590 --> 00:41:53,070
What?

321
00:41:53,070 --> 00:41:57,000
I'm hungry. Will you give me something to eat?

322
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:58,780
Food?

323
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:02,270
We don't have anything. Go out and grab something.

324
00:42:02,270 --> 00:42:04,140
Cook for me.

325
00:42:06,180 --> 00:42:10,170
Do you think I'd be in the mood to cook right now?

326
00:42:10,170 --> 00:42:11,810
Please.

327
00:42:13,740 --> 00:42:17,500
Please. Cook me something.

328
00:42:21,390 --> 00:42:23,460
Do you want an egg in it?

329
00:42:23,460 --> 00:42:26,700
You can put it in. Or not.

330
00:42:30,220 --> 00:42:34,960
I left my son in the ICU.

331
00:42:34,960 --> 00:42:36,230
It's hot.

332
00:42:37,630 --> 00:42:40,120
Do you have to do this to me, Mr. Cha?

333
00:42:46,190 --> 00:42:48,730
What are you doing? Didn't you say you were hungry?

334
00:42:48,730 --> 00:42:50,380
Are you praying?

335
00:42:54,450 --> 00:42:56,320
Thank you.

336
00:42:58,280 --> 00:43:02,350
It's really hard to like you, you know that?

337
00:43:04,060 --> 00:43:09,250
Yun, I'm sorry to have left you. What am I doing here?

338
00:43:40,730 --> 00:43:44,280
There's some rice left over.
Do you want me to give you some?

339
00:43:55,500 --> 00:43:56,780
Mom.

340
00:43:58,530 --> 00:44:03,440
In my next life, I have to be born
as your son once again.

341
00:44:06,500 --> 00:44:14,650
Then I will definitely be a kind-hearted son
who you'll be proud of.

342
00:44:22,170 --> 00:44:23,890
I love you, Mom.

343
00:44:32,970 --> 00:44:34,640
Are you done already?

344
00:44:37,160 --> 00:44:38,430
What's wrong?

345
00:44:41,680 --> 00:44:43,390
It was delicious.

346
00:45:14,280 --> 00:45:16,150
I love you, Mom.

347
00:45:18,020 --> 00:45:19,800
I love you, Mom.

348
00:45:22,490 --> 00:45:28,470
There wasn't a moment that passed
that I didn't love you.

349
00:45:33,590 --> 00:45:35,130
Mom.

350
00:45:36,780 --> 00:45:41,550
Thank you for bringing me into this world.

351
00:46:33,310 --> 00:46:38,300
What's this? He said he was hungry
but barely ate any.

352
00:46:38,300 --> 00:46:42,420
He's so hard to like.

353
00:46:42,420 --> 00:46:45,200
It's really difficult to like him.

354
00:47:06,360 --> 00:47:08,690
What's wrong with me?

355
00:47:13,230 --> 00:47:15,670
Really, what's wrong with me?

356
00:47:52,250 --> 00:47:53,780
Oh! What's that?

357
00:47:53,780 --> 00:47:57,470
Someone sent it special delivery.

358
00:48:00,577 --> 00:48:04,040
[Take this monee and dont releese the book
- Cha Muhyeok]

359
00:48:04,040 --> 00:48:05,870
What does it say?

360
00:48:05,870 --> 00:48:10,980
It asks me to take the money
and not to publish the book.

361
00:48:15,690 --> 00:48:18,990
[Yun Seo-kyeong Bank Book]
Oh! That's my name!

362
00:48:18,990 --> 00:48:20,840
Yun Seo-kyeong. That's my name, right?

363
00:48:20,840 --> 00:48:22,720
Right. It's your name.

364
00:48:23,680 --> 00:48:28,310
It seems that Muhyeok set up
accounts for Galchi and you.

365
00:48:28,310 --> 00:48:34,700
It's for you and Galchi.
It'll last the two of you a lifetime.

366
00:48:36,140 --> 00:48:38,470
I'm gonna publish the book.

367
00:48:38,470 --> 00:48:41,110
I'm going to become rich by publishing the book.

368
00:48:42,440 --> 00:48:43,950
Uncle.

369
00:48:46,010 --> 00:48:49,610
What's wrong? Galchi, why are you crying?

370
00:48:49,610 --> 00:48:53,290
Mom, I think Uncle left.

371
00:48:53,290 --> 00:48:56,850
His clothes and shoes are all gone.

372
00:48:56,850 --> 00:49:00,670
It's like he left us and fled.

373
00:49:00,670 --> 00:49:02,470
Uncle.

374
00:49:02,470 --> 00:49:04,810
Uncle.

375
00:49:04,810 --> 00:49:07,010
Uncle.

376
00:49:08,690 --> 00:49:10,500
What do we do?

377
00:49:30,060 --> 00:49:34,150
It's time to board the plane. Why isn't he here yet?

378
00:49:34,257 --> 00:49:37,324
[Intensive Care Unit]

379
00:49:39,740 --> 00:49:41,310
[Mister Pervert]

380
00:49:48,860 --> 00:49:50,390
Blockhead.

381
00:49:53,320 --> 00:49:55,000
Mister.

382
00:49:56,350 --> 00:49:57,980
I'm sorry.

383
00:50:02,950 --> 00:50:04,530
I love you.

384
00:50:33,970 --> 00:50:35,990
What's so great about me that you'd

385
00:50:36,770 --> 00:50:40,860
come all the way here from Australia?

386
00:50:44,670 --> 00:50:47,450
Okay. Let's date.

387
00:50:52,420 --> 00:50:57,350
Someone said that the saddest people in the world are
the ones without fond memories.

388
00:50:58,510 --> 00:51:06,420
I could live all my life
with just one beautiful memory...

389
00:51:10,900 --> 00:51:12,510
I love you.

390
00:51:14,400 --> 00:51:15,930
I love you.

391
00:51:17,840 --> 00:51:19,550
I love you.

392
00:51:21,540 --> 00:51:23,480
I love you, Mister.

393
00:51:25,400 --> 00:51:29,440
I love you. I love you!

394
00:51:29,440 --> 00:51:33,490
I love you! I love you!

395
00:51:37,990 --> 00:51:41,790
I love you!

396
00:51:41,790 --> 00:51:47,480
I love you!

397
00:51:57,250 --> 00:52:00,450
I'll meet my poor mother one day.

398
00:52:00,450 --> 00:52:03,950
I'll buy her some pretty clothes,
some BBQ meat,

399
00:52:03,950 --> 00:52:05,980
and a beautiful house.

400
00:52:06,910 --> 00:52:11,551
Mom, I'll go there and let you live in luxury.

401
00:52:11,551 --> 00:52:13,210
Just wait five years!

402
00:52:19,110 --> 00:52:22,220
Muhyeok! Son!

403
00:52:22,220 --> 00:52:24,490
My beautiful boy.

404
00:52:24,490 --> 00:52:26,610
My precious son.

405
00:52:28,590 --> 00:52:30,410
I love you.

406
00:52:30,410 --> 00:52:32,200
I love you, son.

407
00:52:52,460 --> 00:52:54,390
[One year later]

408
00:52:54,390 --> 00:52:57,020
He's become much healthier.

409
00:52:57,860 --> 00:53:02,450
He is alive today because
he got his brother's heart, huh?

410
00:53:05,360 --> 00:53:08,880
Why didn't you publish the book?

411
00:53:08,880 --> 00:53:10,590
Because I felt shame.

412
00:53:12,170 --> 00:53:14,720
I'd feel ashamed if I ever saw Muhyeok ever again.

413
00:53:18,230 --> 00:53:22,520
What feud do you have with Audrey?

414
00:53:22,520 --> 00:53:27,340
My little sister's husband got snatched away by Audrey.

415
00:53:27,340 --> 00:53:30,140
He returned to her three years later.

416
00:53:30,140 --> 00:53:36,160
But by then, she was so heartbroken
that she fell ill and died soon thereafter.

417
00:53:40,290 --> 00:53:42,280
He's a pretty good singer.

418
00:53:44,950 --> 00:53:49,660
Audrey is lucky to have such great sons,
don't you think?

419
00:53:55,920 --> 00:53:58,910
[Choi Yun's Comeback Performance]

420
00:54:05,357 --> 00:54:09,047
[Ms. Song Eunchae]

421
00:54:10,980 --> 00:54:13,200
